  "abstract": "<jats:p>The processes of thermochemical hardening of aluminosilicate glass are investigated. The glass was processed in a KNO3 melt under industrial and laboratory conditions at 440…480 °C for 1…120 h. The effect of processing modes on glass properties was evaluated using Vickers microhardness measurement, spectrophotometry, magnetophotoelasticity to measure compressive stresses, and local birefringence analysis to determine the depth of the compressed layer, as well as X-ray fluorescence to evaluate cation exchange. The link between the temperature-time parameters of ion exchange and changes in glass’s structural, mechanical, and optical properties was revealed.</jats:p>",
